        "answer": "No \u2013 reading the current clock inside a calculation introduces a side effect and breaks purity. A pure function must return the same result for the same inputs and have no observable side effects. Reading the clock depends on an external, changing value, so the function\u2019s output can vary even with identical inputs, violating referential transparency.",
