      "answer": {
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "safeHead is preferable to head when a list might be empty because it avoids a runtime error by returning a value of type `Maybe a` that explicitly represents the empty case. The caller must handle the `Nothing` case, making the possibility of an empty list part of the type system and preventing accidental crashes.",
